<title>UK: BA may have to give up one third slots - paper.</title>
<headline>BA may have to give up one third slots - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission is demanding that British Airways give up as many as a third of its slots on U.S. routes from London's Heathrow airport as a condition for approving its proposed alliance with American Airlines, the Independent newspaper reported.</p>
<p>Commission officials are examining the monopoly implications on the tie, which would give the two carriers control of 60 percent of flights between the U.K. and the U.S. and are unlikely to make recommendations before April.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
